description:
Reimplement ImGui's text filter exactly:

```cpp
class TextFilter
{
public:
    explicit TextFilter(const std::string& text);
    bool pass(const std::string& line) const;
};
```

- The filter text is split at commas into **terms**; spaces at the start and end of each term are removed; empty terms are ignored.
- A term starting with `-` is an **exclusion** (the rest of it is the text to look for); any other term is an **inclusion**. A lone `-` is ignored.
- `pass(line)`: if there are no terms, every line passes. Otherwise check the terms **in order**, looking for each one's text inside the line **without regard to case**: the first term found decides: an exclusion returns `false`, an inclusion returns `true`.
- If no term is found in the line: the line passes only if there are **no inclusions** at all.

```
"-missing,texture"   "texture loaded"  -> true;  "texture missing" -> false;  "shader" -> false
"texture,-missing"   "texture missing" -> true   (texture is found first)
"-vsync"             "frame done" -> true;  "vsync on" -> false
```

starter.solution.cpp:
